STEP 1: Liveness with exec (classic demo)
-----------------------------------------
vi probe-liveness.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: liveness-exec
spec:
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "touch /tmp/healthy; sleep 30; rm -f /tmp/healthy; sleep 600"]
    livenessProbe:
      exec:
        command: ["cat", "/tmp/healthy"]
      initialDelaySeconds: 5
      periodSeconds: 5
      failureThreshold: 3

k apply -f probe-liveness.yaml
k get pod liveness-exec -w        # after ~45 s RESTARTS goes to 1, then 2...
k describe pod liveness-exec | grep -A10 Events

Read: "Liveness probe failed: cat: can't open '/tmp/healthy'" then
"Container c failed liveness probe, will be restarted".


STEP 2: Add health endpoints to your app
----------------------------------------
cd ~/k8s-journey/myapp
Edit app.py:

from flask import Flask
import os, socket, time

app = Flask(__name__)
START = time.time()
STARTUP_SECONDS = int(os.environ.get("STARTUP_SECONDS", "0"))
state = {"ready": True, "alive": True}

@app.route("/")
def hello():
    msg = os.environ.get("GREETING", "Hello")
    return f"{msg}! v4 served by {socket.gethostname()}\n"

@app.route("/healthz")
def healthz():
    if time.time() - START < STARTUP_SECONDS:
        return "starting\n", 503
    if not state["alive"]:
        while True:
            time.sleep(1)          # simulate a deadlock: never answers
    return "ok\n"

@app.route("/ready")
def ready():
    return ("ready\n", 200) if state["ready"] else ("not ready\n", 503)

@app.route("/toggle-ready")
def toggle_ready():
    state["ready"] = not state["ready"]
    return f"ready={state['ready']}\n"

@app.route("/hang")
def hang():
    state["alive"] = False
    return "liveness will now hang\n"

app.run(host="0.0.0.0", port=5000, threaded=True)

Build and push as v4:
  docker build -t YOURUSER/myapp:v4 . && docker push YOURUSER/myapp:v4


STEP 3: Deployment with all three probes
----------------------------------------
cd ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week5
vi deploy-probes.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: probed
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: probed}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: probed}
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: app
        image: YOURUSER/myapp:v4
        env:
        - name: STARTUP_SECONDS
          value: "20"
        ports:
        - containerPort: 5000
        startupProbe:
          httpGet: {path: /healthz, port: 5000}
          periodSeconds: 2
          failureThreshold: 30
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet: {path: /healthz, port: 5000}
          periodSeconds: 5
          timeoutSeconds: 2
          failureThreshold: 3
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet: {path: /ready, port: 5000}
          periodSeconds: 3
          failureThreshold: 1
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: probed
spec:
  selector: {app: probed}
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 5000

k apply -f deploy-probes.yaml
k get pods -l app=probed -w

Pods stay 0/1 for ~20 s (startup probe), then 1/1.


STEP 4: Readiness removes a pod from the Service
------------------------------------------------
Terminal 2:
  k get endpointslices -l kubernetes.io/service-name=probed -w

POD=$(k get pods -l app=probed -o name | head -1)
k exec $POD -- python -c "import urllib.request;print(urllib.request.urlopen('http://localhost:5000/toggle-ready').read())"
k get pods -l app=probed           # that pod 0/1, RESTARTS 0

Its IP drops out of the endpoints; traffic only goes to the others:
  k run t --rm -it --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh -c 'for i in $(seq 1 9); do wget -qO- probed; done'
Toggle it back and watch it rejoin.


