STEP 6: Startup probe protects slow starts
------------------------------------------
Set STARTUP_SECONDS to 90 (beyond the 60 s startup budget):
  k set env deploy/probed STARTUP_SECONDS=90
  k get pods -l app=probed -w
New pods get restarted by the startup probe and the rollout stalls;
the old pods keep serving (readiness gates the rollout).
  k rollout undo deploy/probed


STEP 7: Remove the startup probe and see the damage
---------------------------------------------------
Edit deploy-probes.yaml: delete the startupProbe block, keep
STARTUP_SECONDS=20. Apply. The liveness probe now fails during
startup (3 x 5 s = 15 s < 20 s) -> restart loop.
Put the startup probe back and re-apply.


STEP 8: True zero-downtime rollout
----------------------------------
Add to the container (same level as the probes):
        lifecycle:
          preStop:
            exec:
              command: ["sleep", "5"]
Apply. Then run the Day 11/14 traffic loop:
  k run traffic --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh -c 'while true; do wget -qO- -T 1 probed >/dev/null && echo OK || echo FAIL; sleep 0.2; done'
  k rollout restart deploy/probed
  k logs traffic | sort | uniq -c
Expected: zero FAIL.


